Day 2
MariaDB container
first service
▾
Read the Inception subject carefully. Highlight every requirement — there are many small rules.
Set up your project folder structure: srcs/, Makefile, docker-compose.yml, .env file.
Write a Dockerfile for MariaDB using Debian or Alpine (penultimate stable version only — check which).
Write an entrypoint script that initialises the database, creates a user, and sets a password.
Test it in isolation: docker build, docker run, docker exec in and run mysql -u root. Confirm it works alone.
💡 Use environment variables via .env for ALL passwords and usernames. Never hardcode them.

